<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bulgarian Round Table</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bulgarian Round Table was a series of talks in early 1990 between the Bulgarian Communist Party, newly renamed the Socialist Party, and the opposition Union of Democratic Forces. Held after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/todor-zhivkov">Todor Zhivkov</a>'s fall in November 1989, they agreed on multi-party elections to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey">Grand National Assembly</a> in June 1990, which drafted the democratic constitution of 1991.</p></div>
